1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Felipa Colón de Toledo y Mosquera, 2nd Duchess of la Vega, 3rd Duchess of Veragua and 3rd Marchioness of Jamaica (c. 1550 – Valladolid, Olmedo, November 25, 1577), was the second daughter and heiress of Luis Colón 
2 CONC de Toledo, 2nd Duke of Veragua, and first wife María de Mosquera y Pasamonte. She was a great-granddaughter of famous explorer Christopher Columbus.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married her first cousin Diego Colón de Toledo, 4th Admiral of the Indies, without issue. Her husband held that office, which she had inherited, in her place.
