2 CONT
2 CONT Story of a Lineage: The Manuel
2 CONT
2 CONT Wed, 03/11/2010 - 00:56 alexgabriel
2 CONT
2 CONT Image alexgabriel Offline
2 CONT
2 CONT Praetorian Guard
2 CONT
2 CONT From: November 6, 2009 Author: Hasting, 30/Oct/2007 13:17 GMT +1:
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a summary of a research paper I presented at the CSIC conference.
2 CONT
2 CONT The origin of this lineage must be traced back to Ferdinand III King of Castile and Leon, San Fernando from 1671. King D. Fernando was born about the year 1201 and died in 1252, he married Mrs. Beatrice of Swabia who was the daugh
2 CONC ter of Philip of Swabia, King of Germany and Irene Angelo, granddaughter, therefore, the famous Emperor Frederick Barbarossa house HOHENSTAUFFEN and Isaac II Angelus Byzantine family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest son of this marriage was the Infante D. Manuel . According to the testimony of his own son, the famous D. Juan Manuel, in his treatise THAT DON JUAN MANUEL fizo WEAPONS THAT WERE GIVEN TO HIS FATHER ... San Fernando k
2 CONC nowing that it was time to give arms to his son summoned the Archbishop of Sevilla D. Losana Ramon who in his day baptize the infant (this was about sixteen years of age at death of San Fernando). He tells Mr. Villena himself "Arc
2 CONC hbishop devisole these weapons as you bring agora, which are paneled et dyed white and bring them straight as kings. Et on the vermilion cuarterón do walk the golden castiello put him one wing with a gold hand that brings home a s
2 CONC word unsheathed. Et in paneled in white walking the lion put that same lion. Et ... so are our weapons. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Much has been said and brought about the meaning and order of these weapons. Most show the wing with sword in the first and fourth quarters leaving the other to the lions representing the royal arms of the Kingdom of León. Excepti
2 CONC on to this is a seal of a document D. Manuel whose imprint is represented on horseback with drawn sword. In this imprint weapons are just, backwards. First Lions and then the wings, both carrying the knight shield and the horse tr
2 CONC appings. On the reverse the arms is again in the same provision. The stamp is from the year 1253 and is located in the Historical Archive of Madrid.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the significance of these weapons D. Juan Manuel gave an explanation of the virtues that represent each of the pieces in this very explanation of the symbolism of time is unlikely to reality. D. Ramón Menéndez Pidal believed th
2 CONC at it could be a representation of the maternal grandparents Angelo and sword represent the murder of the last emperor of this family. D. Faustino Menéndez - Pidal confirmed the chimeric nature of this explanation.
2 CONT
2 CONT More likely is that the barracks represent the Castilla / León families - Angelo playing with the sound of the words used - wing, manu-el. The sword may be the famous "Lobera" san Fernando, the most precious relic of Manuel and th
2 CONC rough the line of Joanna today is kept in the Royal Armouries Royal Palace of Madrid. Noticeable Infante apart Manor Villena inherited the sword of King Ferdinand with a curious clause and desire ... "Whenever you enter combat vic
2 CONC tory to follow." The clause was that ... "always entered first in battle," thus ensured that their descendants were always named in the chronicles as the heralds had to record the events of the fight and then make a list of the ev
2 CONC ents for the chroniclers.
2 CONT
