2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p22026.htm#i220251
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonora de' Medici
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonora de' Medici (February 28, 1567[1][2] – September 9, 1611) was the eldest child of Francesco I de' Medici and Johanna of Austria. In 1578, when Eleonora was eleven her mother died,[3] and her father later married Bianca Cap
2 CONC pello.[4] Medici was one of seven children. One of her sisters Marie de' Medici became queen of France and was the mother of Louis XIII of France,[5] Marie made her sister Eleonora the godmother of Louis.[6] Eleonora and Marie als
2 CONC o had another sister called Anna who died at the age of 14, the rest of Eleonora and Marie's siblings died during childhood also.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Medici married Vincenzo I Gonzaga on April 29, 1584,[2][8] for her husband it was his second marriage after he divorced Margerita Farnese. Three of her sons would become Dukes of Mantua and Montferrat and her daughter Eleonore wou
2 CONC ld become a Holy Roman Empress. Her children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Francesco IV Gonzaga (May 7, 1586 – December 22, 1612), Duke of Mantua and Duke of Montferrat between February 9 and December 22, 1612.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinando I Gonzaga (April 26, 1587 – October 29, 1626), Duke of Mantua and Duke of Montferrat from 1612 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guglielmo Dominico (1589 – 1591), died during childhood
2 CONT
2 CONT Margerita Gonzaga (2 October 1591 – 7 February 1632) , wife of Henry II, Duke of Lorraine
2 CONT
2 CONT Vincenzo II Gonzaga (January 7, 1594 – December 25, 1627), Duke of Mantua and Marquess of Montferrat from 1626 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonore Gonzaga (September 23, 1598 – June 27, 1655), wife of Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her two daughters were possible second wives to Philip III of Spain, after the death of his wife Margaret of Austria. In 1608 she arranged the marriage of her eldest son Francesco to Margaret of Savoy, this marriage produced three
2 CONC  children, only the eldest daughter Maria reached adulthood, Maria was the mother of Eleanor Gonzaga who became Holy Roman Empress by her marriage to Ferdinand III, Holy Roman Emperor, they were the parents of four children, among
2 CONC  them were Eleonora Maria Josefa of Austria and Maria Anna Josepha, Archduchess of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleonora died on September 9, 1611 in Cavriana, Italy, when she was 44.[9] Her husband outlived her by only one year, dying in 1612.[10], their son Francesco succeeded them, however Francesco was hardly Duke of Mantua for a year b
2 CONC efore his death also in 1612. Francesco was succeeded by his brothers, Eleonora's father died without a surviving male child so his brother Ferdinando succeeded him as Grand Duke of Tuscany.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
