1 NOTE In English, John IV.  He was called The Fortunate.  He was the first of 
2 CONT the Braganza kings. He governed Portugal with energy and ability, 
2 CONT restoring finances and promoting commerce and agriculture. He proclaimed 
2 CONT himself king after driving out the Spanish usurpers in 1640 and finally 
2 CONT routing them at the Battle of Montijo (1644). In 1649 and 1654 the 
2 CONT Portuguese won important naval victories over the Dutch off the coast of 
2 CONT Brazil, thereby regaining their possessions in South America. By his 
2 CONT capable administration, John succeeded in restoring Portugal to a 
2 CONT respected place in Europe.
1 NOTE Joao was crowned and received a new name, Joao IV
1 NOTE KING OF PORTUGAL
