2 CONT http://www.ancestraltrails.ca/walker%20for%20web-o/p788.htm#i51991
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born in Northern Mexico.  His fathers family roots are traced to the old "Hidalgo" families in Andalusia, Spain.  His mother was descended from the noble Onate-Zaldivar family, conquistadors of New Mexico: and the politically entr
2 CONC enched De LA Garza family, Conquistadors of Nuevo Leon, Mexico, who controlled extensive lands from Saltillo to the Rio Grande.  Onate.. was a Spanish Basque Explorer and Zaldivar were Spanish conquistador.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomás Sánchez de la Barrera was a veteran Spanish captain who founded Laredo, Texas, United States, and Nuevo Laredo, Tamaulipas, Mexico, the only town in the Nuevo Santander province.
2 CONT
2 CONT He first arrived in Texas in 1749 to a place he named "El Paso de Jacinto", later called "Indian Ford", which is now west of Downtown Laredo. He then petitioned Colonel José de Escandón, 1st Count of Sierra Gorda for permission to
2 CONC  found a town at this location. His petition was granted on May 15, 1755. He named the new townsite, Villa de San Agustin de Laredo, in honor of Saint Augustine and Colonel Escandon's hometown Laredo, Cantabria, Spain. Don Tomás S
2 CONC ánchez first established three families in the new villa. The site selected is located in the San Agustine Historical District in Downtown Laredo near the San Agustine Cathedral.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT City of Laredo; A Brief History of Laredo, Texas Tomás Sánchez de la Barrera y Garza,  External link
